// Title: Potential File Extension Spoofing Using Right-to-Left Override
// Sigma ID: 979baf41-ca44-4540-9d0c-4fcef3b5a3a4
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Jonathan Peters (Nextron Systems), Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-11-17 | Modified: 2026-03-20
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1036.002
// Description: Detects suspicious filenames that contain a right-to-left override character and a potentially
//   spoofed file extensions.
// False positives:
//   - Filenames that contains scriptures such as arabic or hebrew might make use of this character
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/right-to-left-override/
//   - https://www.malwarebytes.com/blog/news/2014/01/the-rtlo-method
//   - https://tria.ge/241015-l98snsyeje/behavioral2
//   - https://www.unicode.org/versions/Unicode5.2.0/ch02.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_right_to_left_override_extension_spoofing.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\u202e" or FolderPath contains "[U+202E]" or FolderPath contains "‮") and (FolderPath contains "3pm." or FolderPath contains "4pm." or FolderPath contains "cod." or FolderPath contains "fdp." or FolderPath contains "ftr." or FolderPath contains "gepj." or FolderPath contains "gnp." or FolderPath contains "gpj." or FolderPath contains "ism." or FolderPath contains "lmth." or FolderPath contains "nls." or FolderPath contains "piz." or FolderPath contains "slx." or FolderPath contains "tdo." or FolderPath contains "vsc." or FolderPath contains "vwm." or FolderPath contains "xcod." or FolderPath contains "xslx." or FolderPath contains "xtpp.")
